  the framework's OWN predicted slope in the pre-specified window at no external field (e_N = 1.00e-09): +0.503

  the framework's OWN predicted slope in the pre-specified window at 2M++ no-cluster median (e_N = 3.82e-04): +0.898

  the framework's OWN predicted slope in the pre-specified window at 2M++ max-cluster median (e_N = 3.27e-03): +0.985
  [FAIL] K4.1 CANDIDATE 1, the direct form: in the pre-specified deep window -- entirely BELOW the break the framework's own 2M++ external field predicts -- the isolated stack's slope must be near 1 (quenched), not 1/2.  This check fails if it is not   (slope = +0.551 +- 0.040: 11.2 sigma from the quenched 1, 1.3 sigma from the unquenched 1/2)
  [FAIL] K4.2 CANDIDATE 2, the sign test: the framework's EFE requires the higher-external-field (non-isolated) stack to have the STEEPER deep-end slope, d(slope)/d log g_ext > 0.  LambdaCDM's host/two-halo term requires the opposite sign.  This check fails if the difference is not positive   (slope(non-isolated) - slope(isolated) = -0.267 +- 0.045 (6.0 sigma, sign LambdaCDM-like))

