                framework (canonical, 4 calibrations + e_N): chi2 =   812.7/60

  THE THEOREM the environment split was supposed to rest on, stated and then tested:
    any ADDITIVE positive term with a shallower fall-off than the lens's own profile makes the log-log slope
    SHALLOWER, and any MULTIPLICATIVE quench that acts only at low g_bar makes it STEEPER.  LambdaCDM's host and
    two-halo terms are of the first kind, the framework's EFE is of the second, so the SIGN of the difference
    between two environments was claimed to separate them.  Section 8 shows why that claim fails.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
8.  WHY CANDIDATE 2's SIGN IS NOT DEFINITE -- against the candidate, on the framework's OWN physics
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  The deepest bins are at R = 1.29-3.00 Mpc.  A non-isolated lens has a neighbour INSIDE
  that aperture by construction, and in the framework that neighbour carries its own phantom halo, which
  contributes POSITIVELY to Delta_Sigma exactly there.  The framework therefore predicts BOTH a multiplicative
  quench of the lens's own halo AND an additive neighbour term, of opposite signs, and does not predict which
  wins without a model of the neighbour distribution.  Quantitatively:
    mass bin 1: own-halo quench factor at the deepest bin = sqrt(g_bar/(e_N a_0)) = 0.197, i.e. the
                lens's own signal must fall to 19.7% -- yet the measured non-isolated stack is 2.36x the isolated one.
  To produce the measured non-isolated Delta_Sigma = 2.29 Msun/pc^2 at R = 1.29 Mpc the
  neighbour term alone must supply a projected excess mass of 1.21e+13 Msun inside that aperture.
  In the framework a neighbouring GROUP of M_b = 1e13 Msun at 1 Mpc carries a phantom of nu x M_b = 8.70e+13 Msun -- ample.  The escape is open,
  and it is the same escape that candidate 1 named.  CANDIDATE 2's SIGN-DEFINITENESS IS WITHDRAWN.

  ESCAPE QUANTIFIED for candidate 1: refit the ISOLATED stack with a free additive correlated-structure term
  (amplitude free, shape Delta_Sigma ~ R^0.45 as linear theory gives over 0.3-2.6 Mpc) and see how much the
  bound on e_N degrades.
    canonical: with the neighbour term marginalised, 95% bound e_N < 1.04e-04 (was 2.61e-05); the 2M++ median still costs delta chi2 = +28.5
  [FAIL] K8 the escape is quantified rather than asserted: marginalising a free additive correlated-structure term of the shape linear theory gives does NOT rescue the framework's own external field on the isolated stack.  This check fails if the tension survives marginalisation   (delta chi2 at the 2M++ median = +28.5 with the neighbour term free (bound moves +0.60 dex))

